An Untyped's description tells the kernel's own type of the node first below it,
CAP_RETYPED for a pool and CAP_INSTALLED for an installed region, which abi.h does not name.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a description differs from the capability it describes

diff --git a/kernel/object.h b/kernel/object.h
--- a/kernel/object.h
+++ b/kernel/object.h
@@ -323,7 +323,7 @@ static inline uint32_t untyped_made(const struct cap *c)
         return 0;
     }
     uint8_t type = ((const struct cap *)p2v(c->child))->type;
-    return type == CAP_RETYPED ? CAP_POOL : type == CAP_INSTALLED ? CAP_FRAME : type;
+    return type;
 }
 
 static inline struct pool *obj_pool(const struct obj_header *o) { return p2v(o->pool); }
